                            5
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَجَّهَ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He tended, repaired,</i> or <i>betook himself,</i> to, or towards, him, or it, <i>either in a direct
course, or indirectly.</i> (IJ, in M and L, art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قصد</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْمَقُ مَايَتَوَجَّهُ</span>
                        <i>A stupid man, who does
not accomplish his affair well.</i> (JK.)

